				attack bonus (STAB) and a handful of type immunities that turn moves into
				whiffs.
			</p>

			<span class="help-section-title">STAB — same-type attack bonus</span>
			<div class="help-callout">
				<span class="help-callout-eyebrow">1.5× damage</span>
				<span class="help-callout-text">When a Beast uses a move that matches its OWN element, the move deals 1.5× damage. A Fire beast using a Fire move gets +50% on top of any other multipliers.</span>
			</div>
			<p class="help-lead">
				STAB is the reason a Fire move on a Fire beast hits harder than the same Fire
				move on a Neutral beast. When team-building, prefer beasts whose moveset
				leans into their own element.
			</p>

			<span class="help-section-title">Key immunities to remember</span>
			<div class="help-keypoints">
				<div class="help-keypoint">
					<iconify icon="lucide:wind" Size=@(16) Color="#86efac" />
					<span><strong>Wind blocks Earth.</strong> Earth-type attacks deal zero damage to a Wind defender. Brings even a glass-cannon Wind beast back into a fight.</span>
				</div>
				<div class="help-keypoint">
					<iconify icon="lucide:mountain" Size=@(16) Color="#a16207" />
					<span><strong>Earth blocks Electric.</strong> Electric-type attacks deal zero damage to an Earth defender. The cleanest counter to a fast Electric sweeper.</span>
				</div>
				<div class="help-keypoint">
					<iconify icon="lucide:circle" Size=@(16) Color="#9ca3af" />
					<span><strong>Those are the only two.</strong> Every other matchup is just a multiplier — no other type fully blocks another.</span>
